We are now ready to define our main computational problem as follows.

\begin{problem}[\ops]
	Given a plane biconnected graph $G=(V,E)$ and an integer $k$, can we transform $G$ into an outerplane graph $G'$ by applying at most $k$ vertex splits to $G$?
\end{problem}

