   274	\begin{lemma}\label{lem:single-vertex-split}
   275	Let $G$ be a plane biconnected graph and $S \subseteq F$ a subset of the faces $F$ of $G$ that all have the vertex $v \in V$ on their boundary. Then $|S|-1$ splits are sufficient to merge the faces of $S$ into one.
