   292	%To prove that the total number of splits is $|S|-1$, 
   293	We root the tree at an arbitrary face $f' \in S$, which provides a hierarchy on the vertices and faces in $T$.  Every vertex $v \in V(T) \cap V(G)$ requires by \cref{lem:single-vertex-split} $|F'(v)|-1$ splits. Note that that for all leaf vertices in $T$, $|F'(v)|=1$, i.e., they will not be split. Each split is charged to the children of $v$ in $T$. Since $H$ is bipartite, so is $T$. It follows that every face $f \in S \setminus \{ f' \}$ is charged exactly once by its parent, thus $|S|-1$ splits suffice. \qed
