   327	Let $w$ be the subdivision vertex of $(u,v)$ in $G'$. %\mntodo{how do we know $(u,v)$ is an edge? The choice of $u,v$ cannot be arbitrary}
   328	As a subdivision vertex, $w$  is incident to only two faces, one of which, say $f$, must be contained in $S$. 
   329	But $f$ is also incident to $u$ and $v$ and hence $u$ and $v$ are in the same component of $H'$ via face $f$, a contradiction. Hence $H'$ is connected and $S$ is a \cfc of $G'$. \qed
