Implemented and verified a Track B connected-face-cover generator based on the paper’s Section 3 reduction.

Deliverables:

- [gen_2301_09440.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2301.09440/gen_2301_09440.py:1)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2301.09440/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2301.09440/README.md:1)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2301.09440/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2301.09440/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2301.09440/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass, including 0/200,000 random guesses, seven attacks at 0/8, and 120 canonical-key symmetry checks. Additional audits covered 200 exact small graphs and 1,000 generated embeddings.

The external hardening requirement remains blocked: two genuine oracle attempts failed on `easy`, but OpenRouter quota expired before the third attempt. Consequently, no hardened verdict is claimed and the result should not be submitted until the oracle runs complete. This status is documented in the README.

Source: [Splitting Plane Graphs to Outerplanarity](https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.09440).
